# SHA-256 of every file this package carries from its two upstreams: the
# google/re2 C++17 sources at release tag 2025-11-05 (annotated tag object
# b654eab8f96ef2264105343d56d45d0bf1134231, commit
# 927f5d53caf8111721e734cf24724686bb745f55, release tarball SHA-256
# 3b0354b4ff9859c6b9f16ad11b4c600aaa8953c11238582d129f293261e16d54,
# https://github.com/google/re2) and the Abseil LTS 20250512.1 tree, vendored
# whole at vendor/abseil-cpp (commit
# 76bb24329e8bf5f39704eb10d21b9a80befa7c81, release tarball SHA-256
# 9b7a064305e9fd94d124ffa6cc358592eb42b5da588fb4e07d09254aa40086db,
# https://github.com/abseil/abseil-cpp).
#
# That Abseil release is not a version this fork chose on its own. It is the
# one RE2 itself declares at vendor/re2/MODULE.bazel:16 --
# `bazel_dep(name = "abseil-cpp", version = "20250512.1")` -- which is what
# build_support/absl_sources.zig pins and what tools/check-provenance.sh greps
# back out of that file and compares, so the two records cannot drift apart
# silently.
#
# THERE ARE NO SOURCE DEVIATIONS IN THIS TREE. Every vendored byte is the
# upstream byte: one digest per path, no pristine digest kept beside a current
# one, no second digest for any file, and no change notice anywhere under
# vendor/. This is a pristine tree, not a patched one, and the shape of this
# record is the evidence -- a record with two digests per path, or a "compared
# against" note, would be a record of a deviation and there is none here.
#
# To confirm that against upstream rather than take this paragraph's word for
# it, fetch each release archive, check the archive against the digest named
# above, extract it, and compare the whole trees path by path.
#
# THE ENDPOINT MATTERS for RE2, and the reason is inside the archive, so this is
# stated before the commands rather than after a reader has already got a
# different digest. GitHub serves the same commit three ways, and its API
# tarball for a tag names its top-level directory after the TAG OBJECT rather
# than after the tag:
#
#   https://api.github.com/repos/google/re2/tarball/2025-11-05
#       root  google-re2-b654eab/       <- the digest recorded above
#   https://codeload.github.com/google/re2/tar.gz/refs/tags/2025-11-05
#       root  re2-2025-11-05/
#   https://github.com/google/re2/releases/download/2025-11-05/re2-2025-11-05.tar.gz
#       root  re2-2025-11-05/           <- byte-identical to the codeload archive
#
# `google-re2-b654eab` is `b654eab`, the first twelve hex characters of the
# annotated tag object that `refs/tags/2025-11-05` actually points at
# (b654eab8f96ef2264105343d56d45d0bf1134231). The three archives hold identical
# content and differ only in that one directory name, so their digests differ.
# The digest above is the API archive's, because that is the archive this tree
# was vendored from. A reader who fetches from codeload, gets a different digest
# for the same commit and concludes this manifest is wrong, would be right about
# the digest and wrong about the manifest.
#
# The codeload archive and the release asset are a second, independently
# produced archive for the same commit, and both extract to a tree that
# `diff -r` finds identical to vendor/re2. UPSTREAM.md records the digest those
# two share and the observation itself; two sources for one tag agreeing on
# content is what makes "no upstream source file was modified" a result rather
# than a claim. Abseil 20250512.1 has one endpoint and one root name and no such
# ambiguity.
#
#     curl -fsSL -o re2-api.tar.gz \
#       https://api.github.com/repos/google/re2/tarball/2025-11-05
#     printf '%s  %s\n' \
#       3b0354b4ff9859c6b9f16ad11b4c600aaa8953c11238582d129f293261e16d54 \
#       re2-api.tar.gz | sha256sum -c -
#     mkdir -p /tmp/re2-ref && tar -xzf re2-api.tar.gz -C /tmp/re2-ref
#     ls /tmp/re2-ref        # exactly one entry, and it is google-re2-b654eab
#     diff -r /tmp/re2-ref/google-re2-b654eab vendor/re2 && echo "RE2 is pristine"
#
#     curl -fsSL -o absl.tar.gz \
#       https://api.github.com/repos/abseil/abseil-cpp/tarball/20250512.1
#     printf '%s  %s\n' \
#       9b7a064305e9fd94d124ffa6cc358592eb42b5da588fb4e07d09254aa40086db \
#       absl.tar.gz | sha256sum -c -
#     mkdir -p /tmp/absl-ref && tar -xzf absl.tar.gz -C /tmp/absl-ref
#     diff -r /tmp/absl-ref/*/ vendor/abseil-cpp && echo "Abseil is pristine"
#
# The leading `sha256sum -c` in each pair is what makes the reference tree
# demonstrably the pinned archive rather than whatever was downloaded, and the
# `ls` is there because a root directory that is not the one named above means
# the wrong endpoint was fetched -- which is the mistake this block exists to
# catch.
#
# `diff -r` is used without `--no-dereference` because diff(1) here has no such
# option. That costs exactly one thing and it is worth naming: the comparison
# follows vendor/re2/python/LICENSE instead of comparing the link itself. Both
# sides then read the same LICENSE, so the comparison is still content-equal,
# and the record's own view of the link is in group F and in
# tools/check-provenance.sh, which checks the link target directly.
#
# 1671 records, in this exact path set. The path set is the whole of the two
# vendored trees and nothing else: 139 paths under vendor/re2 (138 regular
# files, plus the one symlink vendor/re2/python/LICENSE -> ../LICENSE) and 1532
# under vendor/abseil-cpp. Every file under vendor/ is recorded here and
# nothing outside vendor/ is, which is what lets tools/check-provenance.sh
# answer the question a checksum run cannot: is the vendored set EXACTLY the
# recorded set, with no added, removed or renamed path? A checksum run sees a
# file whose bytes changed; it is blind to a file that was added.
#
#    22  A  RE2 library translation units
#           the set(RE2_SOURCES ...) block at vendor/re2/CMakeLists.txt:113-136
#   19  B  RE2 headers, public and internal
#           every vendor/re2/re2/*.h and every vendor/re2/util/*.h
#  152  C  Abseil library translation units
#           every non-testonly absl_cc_library srcs entry in the vendored tree
#  381  D  Abseil headers and .inc implementation fragments
#           every vendor/abseil-cpp/absl/**.h and **.inc
#    89  E  licence, notice, build and packaging records of both upstreams
#           the two licence texts, the notice files, and the build definitions
#           the source lists of groups A and C were transcribed from
#  1008  F  upstream material retained but not compiled
#           upstream's tests, fuzzers, bindings, generators, benchmarks,
#           documentation, CI and packaging scaffolding, kept so the tree can
#           still be built and audited the way upstream describes
#
# Each group's banner says what that group is and why it is grouped that way;
# they sit immediately above their own records.
#
# Deliberately absent, each for a stated reason. Nothing outside vendor/ is in
# this record at all:
#   build.zig, build.zig.zon, build_support/*.zig, zig/**, runtime/**,
#   tests.zig, smoke.zig, testdata/**, consumer/**
#                     this fork's own build definition, C bridge, Zig facade,
#                     loadable-library runtime, behavioural roots, fixtures and
#                     standalone consumer package. They are rewritten, not
#                     upstream bytes; hashing them would pin a mutable file and
#                     make an ordinary edit look like a supply change. Their
#                     compiled sources and the headers they parse are all
#                     covered above, and the two source lists they carry are
#                     covered by their contents in groups A and C.
#   UPSTREAM.md, NOTICE.md, CHANGELOG.md, FORK-NOTES.md, FORK-LICENSE.md,
#   README.md, README.zig.md, package.nix, flake.nix, flake.lock,
#   devenv.nix, devenv.yaml, .envrc, cross-test.profile.sh,
#   tools/check-provenance.sh, .github/workflows/verify.yml, .gitignore
#                     this fork's own records, licence grant, packaging and CI.
#                     There is no LICENSE at this package root and none is
#                     expected: the fork's grant for its own additions is
#                     FORK-LICENSE.md, the per-file inventory is NOTICE.md, and
#                     the two upstream licence texts are preserved in place at
#                     vendor/re2/LICENSE and vendor/abseil-cpp/LICENSE, which
#                     group E records. There is no README.upstream.md either:
#                     the whole upstream tree is vendored whole under
#                     vendor/re2, so upstream's README is preserved at
#                     vendor/re2/README.md and this fork's README.md is a
#                     different file at a different path, with no collision to
#                     resolve by renaming.
#   UPSTREAM.sha256
#                     a record cannot contain its own digest.
#
# Method: `sha256sum` over each group's path list, from the package root, one
# file at a time, so that every digest is of a file's bytes and not of anything
# assembled. The group boundaries are mechanical and stated above: A and C are
# transcribed from the two `sources` arrays in build_support/, B is `re2/*.h`
# plus `util/*.h`, D is `absl/**.h` plus `**/*.inc`, E is the named licence,
# notice and build-definition set, and F is the remainder of
# `find vendor \( -type f -o -type l \)`. The six groups are disjoint and
# their union is exactly that find.
#
# What this record establishes: if it validates, then the bytes a build
# compiles (A, C), the headers it installs and translates (B, D), the licences
# and build definitions a redistributor must reproduce and that this package
# transcribed its source lists from (E), and the retained upstream material
# that lets the tree still be audited against the releases it came from (F),
# are the bytes pinned here -- and any later edit to any of them fails
# loudly. tools/check-provenance.sh runs this manifest and then checks the
# three things it cannot: that the recorded path set is still exactly the
# vendored one, and that the licences, the release digest and the declared
# Abseil version are still where the records say they are.

#   22  A  RE2 library translation units
#the set(RE2_SOURCES ...) block at vendor/re2/CMakeLists.txt:113-136, in
#upstream's order and spelling, which is verbatim the list in
#build_support/re2_sources.zig `sources`. Nothing else in vendor/re2 is
#compiled into libre2, libre2bridge or re2cpp: not the TESTING_SOURCES list
#below that block (CMakeLists.txt:177-186), not the re2_test/re2_benchmark
#targets, and not the GoogleTest and Google Benchmark downloads
#RE2_BUILD_TESTING would pull in.
