#   381  D  Abseil headers and .inc implementation fragments
#every vendor/abseil-cpp/absl/**.h (357) and **.inc (24). The .inc files are
#not optional, and that is not a claim about style: Abseil sources
#`#include` their implementation fragments by name, so a header tree without
#them cannot compile. 22 of the 24 are reached from files this package
#compiles -- absl/base/internal/spinlock_wait.cc:25-31 includes four
#spinlock_*.inc, absl/debugging/stacktrace.cc:80-88 includes nine
#stacktrace_*-inl.inc, absl/debugging/symbolize.cc:33-43 includes five
#symbolize_*.inc, absl/time/clock.cc:63-65 includes both
#get_current_time_*.inc, and absl/numeric/int128.h:1194,1196 includes
#int128_have_intrinsic.inc and int128_no_intrinsic.inc. The other two,
#absl/log/check_test_impl.inc and absl/log/log_basic_test_impl.inc, are
#reached only from Abseil's own check_test.cc and log_basic_test.cc, which
#are in group F.
