#absl/copts/GENERATED_AbseilCopts.cmake, GENERATED_copts.bzl,
#AbseilConfigureCopts.cmake and configure_copts.bzl together with the two
#scripts that generate them, copts.py and generate_copts.py; and Abseil's own
#CMake packaging definitions CMake/AbseilDll.cmake,
#CMake/AbseilHelpers.cmake, CMake/abslConfig.cmake.in, CMake/README.md and
#the two Googletest files CMake/Googletest/CMakeLists.txt.in and
#DownloadGTest.cmake. The per-directory BUILD.bazel and CMakeLists.txt
#blocks are the `srcs` lists this package transcribed group C from, so a
#drift between them and build_support/absl_sources.zig is a drift this
#record makes visible; the copts tables are the flags it transcribed into
#build_support/platform_flags.zig. Abseil 20250512.1 ships no NOTICE file:
#its AUTHORS names Google Inc. and the Apache-2.0 text in its LICENSE is the
#notice that travels. No third-party code is compiled into any of the three
#published libraries -- libre2, libre2bridge and the re2cpp C++ runtime --
