#   1008  F  upstream material retained but not compiled
#RE2: the whole re2/testing/** tree (32 files, upstream's own GoogleTest
#suite), re2/fuzzing/re2_fuzzer.cc (a libFuzzer entry point, which needs a
#fuzzing toolchain rather than a compiler), python/** (8: the pybind11
#bindings, their tests and setup.py), app/** (9: the WASM/JavaScript demo),
#benchlog/** (6), doc/** (5), the four generator scripts that produce the
#compiled table sources (re2/make_perl_groups.pl, make_unicode_casefold.py,
#make_unicode_groups.py and unicode.py, which Makefile:268,272 uses to
#regenerate re2/perl_groups.cc, unicode_casefold.cc and unicode_groups.cc),
#util/pcre.cc, runtests, testinstall.cc, lib/git/commit-msg.hook, .bcr/**
#(3) and .github/** (9). Abseil: ci/** (18),
#CMake/install_test_project/** (3), .github/** (3), .gitignore,
#absl/abseil.podspec.gen.py, absl/base/c_header_test.c,
#absl/flags/flag_benchmark.lds, all 230 *_test.cc, all 46 *_benchmark.cc,
#the 19 remaining library-shaped .cc files that are none of those and are not
#compiled, and the 603-file CCTZ timezone corpus at
#absl/time/internal/cctz/testdata/**.
#
#The 19: 14 of them are the `excluded` table in
#build_support/absl_sources.zig, each with the declaring `testonly` or
#GoogleTest statement it was dropped for. The other three entries of that
#table -- absl/base/internal/spinlock_benchmark.cc,
#absl/synchronization/mutex_benchmark.cc and
#absl/synchronization/internal/per_thread_sem_test.cc -- are already counted
#above, as a *_benchmark.cc and a *_test.cc. Five of the 19 are in no table,
#because no table claims them: absl/flags/flag_test_defs.cc and
#absl/hash/internal/print_hash_of.cc, which upstream declares only for its
#own tests, and the three benchmark-shaped units
#absl/random/benchmarks.cc, absl/random/internal/randen_benchmarks.cc and
#absl/random/internal/gaussian_distribution_gentables.cc, which are named
#like library sources and are not reached by any *_benchmark.cc. Naming the
#set here rather than leaving it to be counted is deliberate: it is exactly
#the set that would otherwise look like an accidental omission from group C.
#
#One entry is a symlink rather than a regular file:
#vendor/re2/python/LICENSE -> ../LICENSE, the only symlink in either
#vendored tree. Its recorded digest is therefore NECESSARILY the same 64 hex
#characters as the record for vendor/re2/LICENSE, because the digest is of
#the bytes the link resolves to. That equality is the correct result and not
#a copy-paste error; a reader expecting two different digests here is looking
#at the wrong thing. It is listed in this group rather than group E because
#the pybind11 bindings it licenses are retained material this package does
#not build.
#
#These are retained so the tree can still be built and audited the way
#upstream describes: upstream's own CMake and Bazel builds, its `make test`,
#its generators and its CI scripts all resolve into these paths, and deleting
#them would make this fork's tree a different distribution from the release
#it claims to carry. They are recorded for that reason and for no other:
#NOTHING in this group is compiled, installed, linked, run or read by any
#gate of this package.
